feature: current-user-display-logout
description: |
  Build a complete "Current User Display and Logout" feature (FE + BE).
  FE: add a user profile section on the far-right of the top navigation bar that
  displays the current logged-in user's name/email, plus a functional "Log Out"
  button (next to the name or in a dropdown). Clean, modern UI/UX.
  BE + Integration: create a backend endpoint (POST /api/auth/logout) to handle
  session invalidation / token revocation securely; FE calls the logout endpoint,
  clears local state/tokens (localStorage/cookies), and redirects to /login.
created: 2026-09-02
status: proposed
phases:
  - specify: pending
  - plan: pending
  - tasks: pending
  - implement: pending
  - analyze: pending
  - converge: pending
kb_snapshot:
  constitution_loaded: true
  architecture_loaded: true
  design_loaded: true
  modules_affected:
    - Auth (Hoàng) — backend acknowledgement endpoint + contract update
    - Frontend (shell: Phương) — top-bar user section, logout wiring
  contracts_affected:
    - kb/contracts/auth.yaml (POST /api/auth/logout, GET /api/auth/me)
  related_adrs:
    - ADR-0015 (Supabase Auth)
    - ADR-0016 (app-level userId filtering)
  key_constraint: >
    Auth is Supabase-based with stateless JWTs verified via JWKS; the backend holds
    no session store. Secure logout is driven by supabase.auth.signOut() (invalidates
    refresh token + clears cookies). POST /api/auth/logout is a guarded acknowledgement
    endpoint (Constitution IV Simplicity — no token denylist). Contract V: interface
    change requires a contract + module-doc update.
